<Base
  title="My Story"
  description="A short introduction to how Prateek Alakh thinks about curiosity, learning, and building."
>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">My Story</p>
    <h1 class="story-title">
      There's always another<br />
      <em>story</em> waiting to be found.
    </h1>
  </header>

  <article class="prose section">
    <p>I enjoy understanding how things work, discovering why things are the way they are, and imagining how they could be different.</p>

    <p>That curiosity often takes me in unexpected directions. It might lead me into technology, history, or a fictional world I'm completely immersed in. Sometimes, it's as simple as discovering the story behind an ordinary object.</p>

    <p>I enjoy creating things, solving problems, and finding ways to make everyday experiences a little better. There's something rewarding about taking an idea and giving it life.</p>

    <p>And not all discoveries happen behind a screen. Exploring a new place, getting out on a trail, or trying something I've never done before can be just as exciting.</p>

    <p>I find that there's something interesting to take away from almost every experience. Sometimes it's a new perspective, sometimes a new skill, and sometimes simply a good story.</p>
    
    <p>This website is a small collection of those stories, experiences, ideas and things I've brought to life.</p>


    

    <aside class="aside">
      <p class="kicker">Work</p>
      <p>
        I work across software, infrastructure, and automation, especially where a complicated system can be made simpler, more reliable, and easier to use.
      </p>
      <p>A few of those projects are in <a href="/built">Things I've Built</a>.</p>
    </aside>
  </article>

  <a class="pager" href="/built">
    <small>Next</small>
    <span>Things I've Built</span>
  </a>
</Base>
